## Continuation: epochs 13-18

At the user's request the run continues to 18 epochs, with the same scheme as the dense-1/8 run. An online
producer cannot resume and the 12-epoch cosine schedule decays to 0, so epochs 13-18 are a separate launch on the
same corpus, recipe and layout (`scripts/launch/dense-same/continue_node.sh`, started on the trainer node and
waiting until the 12-epoch run has finished cleanly):

| | |
| --- | --- |
| start | weights-only warm start from the epoch-12 (final) checkpoint of `dense-same`; AdamW state is reset |
| LR schedule | 1% warm-up to **2e-4** (1/3 of the original peak), cosine to 0 over the 6 epochs (about 66,600 steps) |
| prompt order | `training.prompt_seed: 54` (epochs 1-12 used 42) |
| run id / output | `dense-same-ep13-18`, `/scratch/dense/outputs/dense-same-ep13-18`, checkpoint every 11,100 steps |
| W&B | the same run (`dense-same-r6`, `WANDB_RESUME=allow`) with `SPECFORGE_TRACKING_STEP_OFFSET=133200` (= 12 x 11,100), so the curve continues at step 133,200 instead of restarting; `train/segment_optimizer_step` holds the continuation's own step (tracking code identical to dense-1/8, commit 3375bc9) |
| exports | `13ep/` ... `18ep/` on HF, recorded below at global step 133,200 + 11,100 x k |

Expect a small dip in train/acc right after epoch 12 while the LR warms up again.

## Acceptance-length benchmark (protocol of jiapingW/Qwen3-8b-dspark-SpecForge)

Run on the capture node (rank 0) next to the capture servers, which are idle most of the time (training speed was
checked to be unchanged): `scripts/launch/dense-same/bench_all.sh` / `bench_node.sh` / `bench_accept.py`.

| | |
| --- | --- |
| requests per mode | 2400: GSM8K 1319, MATH500 500, HumanEval 164, MBPP (sanitized test) 257, MT-Bench 80 two-turn conversations (160 requests, turn 2 carries the model's own turn-1 answer) |
| prompts | SpecForge benchmark formats, Qwen3 chat template, thinking off, no system prompt, max_new_tokens 2048 |
| server | SGLang 0.5.18 (image `lmsysorg/sglang:v0.5.18-cu130` + spec-capture patch; jiapingW used 0.5.21 with his own adapter), DSPARK, bf16, TP1, flashinfer target attention, context 16384, max_running_requests 1, CUDA graphs and radix cache off, one server per GPU |
| widths | D16/V16 = anchor + 15 candidates (`--speculative-dspark-block-size 15`), D16/V8 = anchor + 7 (`7`); with the causal draft block the first k candidates equal the first k of the 16-token block |
| temperature 1 | top_p 1, top_k -1, `sampling_seed = 42 + uint32_le(SHA256(dataset:sample_id:turn)[:4])`; SGLang's own DSpark sampling verification (jiapingW used a process-local overlay), so t=1 numbers are comparable between checkpoints run here, less so to his published t=1 values |
| metric | per request tau = completion_tokens / spec_verify_ct; request macro = mean over requests, micro = total tokens / total verify rounds |

Checkpoints: jiapingW's published step-39000 drafter (also re-measured here to validate the harness) and our epoch-12 export.

